Minimal-description-length scoring and decomposition (src/normalize/mdl.rs)
==========================================================================

Source:  https://github.com/mutalyzer/description-extractor
Commit:  155b79d29c4f74c32dfcb4ae3096a4a5a3b009bb
License: MIT (Leiden University Medical Center)

`src/normalize/mdl.rs` is a Rust port of the C++ algorithm in that
repository's `extractor/extractor.{h,cc}` (author: Jonathan K. Vis),
specifically the DNA path: `extract`, `extractor`, `LCS`, `LCS_1`,
`LCS_k`, `prefix_match`, `suffix_match`, `string_match`,
`string_match_reverse` and `IUPAC_complement`, together with the weight
table from `extractor.h:100-106` and the `weight_position` derivation at
`extractor.cc:100-103`.

It is a port, not a copy: no upstream source text is reproduced in the
Rust file, which cites upstream line numbers instead. The upstream MIT
licence requires attribution; this file satisfies that requirement. See
the upstream LICENSE for the full text.

What is DELIBERATELY NOT ported
-------------------------------
* `extractor_transposition` and the `TRANSPOSITION_OPEN`/`_CLOSE`
  variant types (`extractor.cc:516-655`). ferro's `Piece` carries a
  literal replacement and has no cross-reference spelling, so a
  transposition has nowhere to land. Every site that would have called
  it takes the branch the C++ takes when the transposition is rejected
  — see `mdl.rs`'s module doc for the exact list.
* `extractor_protein`, `extractor_frame_shift`, `LCS_frame_shift`,
  `backtranslation` and the codon/frame-shift maps: the protein path.
* The `Variant::probability` union member and `debug.cc`/`sandbox.cc`.

What is PARAMETERIZED beyond upstream
-------------------------------------
Upstream hard-codes its weight table, derives `weight_position` from the
whole reference length, and applies its collapse test greedily. All
three are exposed here as `mdl::Config` knobs, with the upstream values
as the documented default (`Config::MUTALYZER`), because they are
calibration rather than principle. See `mdl.rs`.

Ported test cases
-----------------
`mdl::tests::upstream` replays the 18 `(reference, sample) -> variant
list` cases from the upstream `tests/test_extractor.py` at the commit
above, and the description-level expectations from
`tests/test_describe.py`. Those files are MIT under the same licence.
